( gossip.tal — trace/presence gossip, ROM to ROM, over the step-3 datagram lane. )
(                                                                                        )
( WHAT IT IS FOR. The mesh's coordination has always needed a shell on at least one end: )
( mesh-uxn-hop's pipe lane wants ssh, an account and bash on the far node, and the board )
( is a file one node owns. This receiver needs none of that — a node holding only uxncli )
( is a full participant, which is exactly what makes the phone a peer rather than the )
( weak link somebody with a shell has to poll. )
(                                                                                        )
( input  : two lines on stdin — line 1 the bind address 'udp:host:port' [a NAMED address; )
(          the device refuses every spelling of the any-address on this lane], line 2 the )
(          ledger path to merge into. )
( wire   : one datagram = one row, '<id> <rest of the row>'. The id is the FIRST field, )
(          space-terminated, 1..16 bytes, and it is the whole of the identity. )
( reply  : 'uxn:new <id>' merged · 'uxn:dup <id>' already held · 'uxn:bad <id>' unparseable )
(          · 'uxn:ful <id>' the ledger outgrew the scan window · 'uxn:err <id>' the append )
(          did not land [the file device sandboxes to the CWD — a ledger outside it is )
(          refused with a count of zero, and a merge that cannot write must not say 'new']. )
(          The same verdict )
(          goes to stdout, so the decision is observable from BOTH ends of the wire. )
( output : "NA" rc 2 — bind refused or nothing arrived · "NODEV" rc 3 — no device/too old. )
(                                                                                        )
( IDEMPOTENCE IS THE WHOLE CONTRACT, not a nicety. Anyone who can see a packet can replay )
( it — the hop lane's token is replayable by construction — so a receiver that appends what )
( it is handed is a write amplifier aimed at its own ledger by whoever felt like it. Every )
( row is therefore checked against the ledger ITSELF before it is written: the id must not )
( already start a line there. Not a "recently seen" ring — a bounded memory of ids means a )
( replay that arrives after eviction is merged again, and "idempotent for a while" is not a )
( property anything can rely on. )
(                                                                                        )
( AND WHEN IT CANNOT DECIDE, IT REFUSES. The scan window is 16 KB. A ledger larger than )
( that cannot be searched in one read, so this ROM does NOT append — it answers 'ful' and )
( leaves the row alone. The tempting alternative, treating an unsearchable ledger as "not )
( seen", turns the one guarantee here off silently at exactly the size where duplicates )
( start to matter. A pruner keeps the file small; a receiver that guesses does not. )
(                                                                                        )
( THE ID IS THE SENDER'S. This ROM does not hash the row: a checksum computed here would )
( make two spellings of one event two events, and it cannot see what the sender meant. It )
( is also NOT authentication — nothing here is. On this lane authentication is the tailnet )
( ACL and the named bind address, which is why the device refuses to bind anything else. )
(                                                                                        )
( zero-page: line=00 tries=01 ptr=02 got=04 scanlen=06 p=08 i=0a j=0c idlen=0e )
(            packets=10 found=11 )

|0100
    #0000 #d4 DEO2           ( clear the length register: a device-less page reads this back )
    #d0 #da DEO              ( action d0 Identify — only the DEVICE answers )
    #d4 DEI #d0 NEQ ,&nodev JCN
    #d5 DEI #03 LTH ,&nodev JCN   ( the datagram bind arrived in step 3, compared as an )
                                  ( ORDERING so every later step still satisfies this ROM )
    ;on-console #10 DEO2
    ;uri-buf #02 STZ2
    #00 #00 STZ              ( line 0: the bind address )
    BRK
    &nodev ;no-dev JMP2

@on-console
    #12 DEI
    DUP #0a EQU ,&nl JCN
    #02 LDZ2 STA
    #02 LDZ2 INC2 #02 STZ2
    BRK
    &nl
    POP
    #00 #02 LDZ2 STA         ( NUL-terminate the line in place )
    #00 LDZ #00 EQU ,&first JCN
    ;serve JMP2
    &first
    #01 #00 STZ              ( line 1: the ledger path )
    ;path-buf #02 STZ2
    BRK

@serve
    #01 #df DEO              ( SELECT the lane first — a datagram bind takes exactly this )
                             ( channel, and channel 0 is the outbound lane )
    ;uri-buf #dd DEO2
    #db DEI2 #0000 EQU2 ,&norun JCN   ( the handle is the ONE read that touches no socket, )
                             ( so a refused bind is caught without spending a deadline )
    #08 #10 STZ              ( serve at most 8 rows, then halt: a ROM that never returns is )
                             ( a wedge, and a keeper re-runs this far more cheaply than a )
                             ( watchdog can prove a loop is alive )
    ;wait JMP2
    &norun ;na JMP2

@wait
    #03 #01 STZ              ( three deadlines of patience per row )
    &poll
    #da DEI                  ( WAITS — the device's deadline, never a spin, and on a )
                             ( datagram lane this read does NOT consume the packet )
    DUP #03 EQU ,&packet JCN ( HasData )
    #06 EQU ,&idle JCN       ( Bound: up, nobody sent yet )
    ;na JMP2                 ( Unbound: the socket is gone )
    &idle
    #01 LDZ #01 SUB #01 STZ
    #01 LDZ #00 EQU ,&spent JCN
    ,&poll JMP
    &spent ;finish JMP2
    &packet POP ;recv JMP2

@recv
    #00ff #d4 DEO2           ( 255 bytes: a row longer than this is DISCARDED by the device )
                             ( and said so, never delivered short )
    ;in-buf #d6 DEO2
    #d4 DEI2 #04 STZ2
    #04 LDZ2 #0000 EQU2 ,&next JCN   ( an empty packet is not a row — and it is NOT a close )
    ;parse-id JSR2
    #0e LDZ2 #0000 EQU2 ,&bad JCN
    ;scan-ledger JSR2
    #11 LDZ #02 EQU ,&full JCN
    #11 LDZ #00 NEQ ,&dup JCN
    ;append-row JSR2
    #a2 DEI2 #04 LDZ2 NEQ2 ,&err JCN  ( THE WRITE IS CHECKED, always: the file device )
                             ( sandboxes to the CWD and answers a blocked path with a )
                             ( warning on stderr and a count of zero, so a ledger outside )
                             ( the sandbox would otherwise be answered 'new' forever while )
                             ( nothing was ever written — a merge that reports success and )
                             ( leaves no artifact. A short write is not a success either. )
    ;v-new ;reply JSR2
    ,&next JMP
    &err  ;v-err ;reply JSR2 ,&next JMP
    &dup  ;v-dup ;reply JSR2 ,&next JMP
    &bad  ;v-bad ;reply JSR2 ,&next JMP
    &full ;v-ful ;reply JSR2
    &next
    #10 LDZ #01 SUB #10 STZ
    #10 LDZ #00 EQU ,&fin JCN
    ;wait JMP2
    &fin ;finish JMP2

( parse-id: idlen := the offset of the first space, or 0 if there is none, if it is the )
( first byte, or if it runs past 16. A row whose identity cannot be read is refused rather )
( than merged under some substitute the sender never chose. )
@parse-id
    #0000 #0a STZ2
    &l
    #0a LDZ2 #04 LDZ2 EQU2 ,&none JCN
    ;in-buf #0a LDZ2 ADD2 LDA #20 EQU ,&hit JCN
    #0a LDZ2 INC2 #0a STZ2
    ,&l JMP
    &hit
    #0a LDZ2 #0e STZ2
    #0a LDZ2 #0000 EQU2 ,&none JCN
    #0a LDZ2 #0011 LTH2 ,&ok JCN
    &none #0000 #0e STZ2
    &ok
    JMP2r

( scan-ledger: found := 1 if a line in the ledger STARTS with the id followed by a space, )
( 2 if the ledger is too large to search, 0 if it is not there. Line-anchored on purpose: )
( an id that merely appears somewhere in a row's text is a different fact. )
@scan-ledger
    #00 #11 STZ
    ;path-buf #a8 DEO2       ( name the file — the low byte opens it )
    #4000 #aa DEO2
    ;scan-buf #ac DEO2       ( the low byte of the read port transfers )
    #a2 DEI2 #06 STZ2
    #06 LDZ2 #0000 EQU2 ,&out JCN     ( no ledger yet, or empty: nothing can be held )
    #06 LDZ2 #4000 EQU2 ,&full JCN    ( filled the window — we CANNOT say "not there" )
    #0000 #08 STZ2
    &line
    ;match JSR2
    #11 LDZ #00 NEQ ,&out JCN
    &adv
    #08 LDZ2 #06 LDZ2 EQU2 ,&out JCN
    ;scan-buf #08 LDZ2 ADD2 LDA #0a EQU ,&nl2 JCN
    #08 LDZ2 INC2 #08 STZ2
    ,&adv JMP
    &nl2
    #08 LDZ2 INC2 #08 STZ2
    #08 LDZ2 #06 LDZ2 EQU2 ,&out JCN
    ,&line JMP
    &full #02 #11 STZ
    &out
    JMP2r

( match: does the ledger at p hold <id><space>? )
@match
    #08 LDZ2 #0e LDZ2 ADD2 INC2 #06 LDZ2 GTH2 ,&no JCN
    #0000 #0c STZ2
    &m
    #0c LDZ2 #0e LDZ2 EQU2 ,&tail JCN
    ;scan-buf #08 LDZ2 ADD2 #0c LDZ2 ADD2 LDA
    ;in-buf #0c LDZ2 ADD2 LDA
    NEQ ,&no JCN
    #0c LDZ2 INC2 #0c STZ2
    ,&m JMP
    &tail
    ;scan-buf #08 LDZ2 ADD2 #0e LDZ2 ADD2 LDA #20 NEQ ,&no JCN
    #01 #11 STZ
    &no
    JMP2r

( append-row: one row, newline-terminated, appended. The terminator is enforced here )
( because a row without one merges the NEXT row into its own line, and the id of the next )
( row then starts no line at all — the dedupe would go blind to it forever after. )
@append-row
    ;in-buf #04 LDZ2 ADD2 #0001 SUB2 LDA #0a EQU ,&has JCN
    #0a ;in-buf #04 LDZ2 ADD2 STA
    #04 LDZ2 INC2 #04 STZ2
    &has
    #01 #a7 DEO              ( append, never truncate )
    ;path-buf #a8 DEO2
    #04 LDZ2 #aa DEO2
    ;in-buf #ae DEO2
    #00 #a7 DEO
    JMP2r

( reply: 'uxn:' + a 4-byte verb + the id, to the SENDER — an address this ROM never names, )
( because the device recorded it — and the same line to stdout, so the verdict is readable )
( from either end and a gate does not have to trust one of them. )
@reply ( verb* -- )
    #0000 #0a STZ2
    &v
    LDAk ;out-body #0a LDZ2 ADD2 STA
    INC2
    #0a LDZ2 INC2 #0a STZ2
    #0a LDZ2 #0004 NEQ2 ,&v JCN
    POP2
    #0000 #0c STZ2
    &i
    #0c LDZ2 #0e LDZ2 EQU2 ,&d JCN
    ;in-buf #0c LDZ2 ADD2 LDA
    ;out-body #0004 ADD2 #0c LDZ2 ADD2 STA
    #0c LDZ2 INC2 #0c STZ2
    ,&i JMP
    &d
    #0e LDZ2 #0008 ADD2 #d4 DEO2
    ;out-buf #d8 DEO2
    #0000 #0c STZ2
    &e
    #0c LDZ2 #0e LDZ2 #0004 ADD2 EQU2 ,&z JCN
    ;out-body #0c LDZ2 ADD2 LDA #18 DEO
    #0c LDZ2 INC2 #0c STZ2
    ,&e JMP
    &z
    #0a #18 DEO
    JMP2r

@finish
    #80 #0f DEO              ( halt, exit 0 )
    BRK

@na
    ;na-str ;emit JSR2
    #82 #0f DEO              ( halt, exit 2 — a claim about the LINK )
    BRK

@no-dev
    ;nodev-str ;emit JSR2
    #83 #0f DEO              ( halt, exit 3 — a claim about THIS EMULATOR, not the link )
    BRK

@emit ( str* -- )
    &l LDAk #00 EQU ,&d JCN
    LDAk #18 DEO INC2 ,&l JMP
    &d POP2
    JMP2r

@na-str "NA 0a 00
@nodev-str "NODEV 0a 00
@v-new "new 20
@v-dup "dup 20
@v-bad "bad 20
@v-ful "ful 20
@v-err "err 20

( the tag is DATA and every buffer after it is a pad, so it goes FIRST: bytes written past )
( the last pad set the ROM's length. )
@out-buf   "uxn 3a
@out-body  $40
@uri-buf   $80
@path-buf  $80
@in-buf    $100
@scan-buf  $4000
